Subject: [PATCH] build: upgrade dependencies including x/net and OpenTelemetry advisories

SeaweedFS 4.40 pins vulnerable gRPC, etcd, Thrift, x/image, x/crypto and
x/net versions. gRPC 1.83.2 includes fixes for GHSA-hrxh-6v49-42gf,
GHSA-vp52-pcj8-j9qc, and GHSA-2v4p-qf9q-27wj. The etcd client, transport,
and API modules move together to 3.6.14 for GO-2026-6107. x/image 0.45.0
fixes GO-2026-6222; x/crypto 0.57.0 fixes GO-2026-6303, GO-2026-6354,
and GO-2026-6355, reachable through weed/sftpd. x/net 0.60.0 fixes
GO-2026-6603, GO-2026-6610, GO-2026-6611, GO-2026-6612 and GO-2026-6617,
reachable through the HTTP/2 transport; the other x/ modules move with it.

OpenTelemetry SDK and trace exporters move together to 1.45.0 to fix
GO-2026-6505.

Thrift 0.24.0 includes GHSA-8wv5-x4w7-5gww and the 32-bit range fix
previously pinned by the upstream replace directive, so that replace is
removed. Go resolves the transitive dependency upgrades. x/crypto requires
Go 1.26, so the module directive moves to 1.26.0 and the Eneo builder
tracks Go 1.26. Keep this patch until an upstream SeaweedFS release
includes these dependency versions or newer.

